From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seilent <github@seilent.net>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:08:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: ucsi: Fix the USB data check on partner change

Since commit 0c8ee850572b ("usb: typec: ucsi: Add UCSI_USB4_IMPLIES_USB
quirk for X1E80100"), ucsi_partner_change() clears the USB role of a
partner without the USB flag only on platforms with the
UCSI_USB4_IMPLIES_USB quirk. On every other platform a partner without
USB data, such as a USB PD charger that the PPM reports as a DFP, gets
a data role on a connector change, and the USB controller is switched
to device mode for it. ucsi_register_port() gives the same partner no
role.

Check for USB data in one helper used by both paths: a partner supports
USB data when it sets the USB flag, or, with UCSI_USB4_IMPLIES_USB, when
it reports USB4 Gen 3 or Gen 4. ucsi_register_port() now honors the
quirk too, so on X1E80100 a USB4 dock without the USB flag that is
connected when the port registers gets its role.

Fixes: 0c8ee850572b ("usb: typec: ucsi: Add UCSI_USB4_IMPLIES_USB quirk for X1E80100")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: seilent <github@seilent.net>
---
 drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c | 18 ++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
index 5aab8ab9f0132..90a703aa76b95 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
@@ -1326,6 +1326,16 @@ static void ucsi_unregister_partner(struct ucsi_connector *con)
 	con->partner = NULL;
 }
 
+static bool ucsi_partner_supports_usb(struct ucsi_connector *con)
+{
+	if (UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB))
+		return true;
+
+	return (con->ucsi->quirks & UCSI_USB4_IMPLIES_USB) &&
+	       (UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB4_GEN3) ||
+		UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB4_GEN4));
+}
+
 static void ucsi_partner_change(struct ucsi_connector *con)
 {
 	enum usb_role u_role = USB_ROLE_NONE;
@@ -1367,10 +1377,7 @@ static void ucsi_partner_change(struct ucsi_connector *con)
 			typec_partner_set_usb_mode(con->partner, USB_MODE_USB4);
 	}
 
-	if ((!UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB)) &&
-	    ((con->ucsi->quirks & UCSI_USB4_IMPLIES_USB) &&
-	     (!(UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB4_GEN3) ||
-		UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB4_GEN4)))))
+	if (!ucsi_partner_supports_usb(con))
 		u_role = USB_ROLE_NONE;
 
 	ret = usb_role_switch_set_role(con->usb_role_sw, u_role);
@@ -1963,8 +1970,7 @@ static int ucsi_register_port(struct ucsi *ucsi, struct ucsi_connector *con)
 			ucsi_check_cable(con);
 	}
 
-	/* Only notify USB controller if partner supports USB data */
-	if (!(UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB)))
+	if (!ucsi_partner_supports_usb(con))
 		u_role = USB_ROLE_NONE;
 
 	ret = usb_role_switch_set_role(con->usb_role_sw, u_role);
-- 
